n['review'](r,p,'Full442-line guide and all exact block occurrences read. Quality-constrained cost objective; check caching/config before comparisons and measured per-cell billing/usage; model×effort search names tier-monotonicity and cost assumptions, conservative uncertainty-aware inclusion and matched-profile deferral/reopening; noisy near-floor pass/fail repeats before pruning; costly quality reference separately declared; prompt tuning frozen to selected model, re-probe earlier failed cells after changed context, fresh joint confirm of model/prompt/setting with preregistered quality/cost/mechanism gates; selection set distinguished from true holdout, baseline/build variance, forecasts/falsifiers before measurements, whole-traffic router evaluation; engagement census excludes prompt echoes; instruction mass vs actions and output-quality tradeoffs. Numerous self-described internal measured programs, percentages, token/cost ratios, data-retention/API/effort/cache facts and model/topology superiority are unsupported by locatable raw experiments in this repo and are not admitted as efficacy. Cost/quality monotonicity can fail; fixed sample counts and best-baseline-repeat floor do not establish noninferiority. Constant action counts need not imply ignored preventive text; literal marker subtraction is weaker than actual tool-result evidence. “Near-zero engagement means dead weight” and cheaper-help-never-addition are overbroad. Pruning/search heuristics do not guarantee the best untested cell; apparent mechanism alone does not establish robustness.',[k1,k2,'core-anthro-heldout-channel','core-counter-semantics-before-totals'])
